<title>USA: Terex Corp Q3 shr loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Terex Corp Q3 shr loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>WESTPORT, Conn. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $0.06     loss	 $0.93</p>
<p> Net	profit	  1,400     loss	 7,800</p>
<p> Sales		    276,400		  283,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,200		   10,300</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr     profit  $0.03	     loss $3.75</p>
<p> Net     profit  6,400	     loss 33,400</p>
<p> Sales	     856,600		  766,900</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  13,000		   10,300</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Table based on pro forma results including those of discontinued operations. Earnings from continuing operations were a $0.40 per share loss for the 1996 third quarter, compared to a $1.36 per share loss for the year-ago quarter.</p>
<p>The company has announced its intention to dispose of its Material Handling Segment but included the segment in third quarter results to provide continuity with prior results.</p>
</text>
